    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The genus Cupressus is one of several genera within the family Cupressaceae that have the common name cypress; for the others, see cypress. It is considered a polyphyletic group. Based on genetic and morphological analysis, the \"Cupressus\" genus is found in the Cupressoideae subfamily. The common name comes from Old French \"cipres\" and that from Latin \"cyparissus\", which is the latinisation of the Greek κυπάρισσος (\"kypárissos\").",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
